From: "JQE Chief Engineer (Claude)" <jqe-bot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] feat: add BrokerGateway abstract interface and shared
 DTOs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

broker/types.py defines the only shapes any gateway implementation may
cross with: AccountInfo, Candle, Tick, OrderRequest, OrderResult,
Position, TradeHistoryEntry (Pydantic models, validated + JSON-
serializable for free), plus Timeframe/OrderSide/OrderType/OrderStatus
enums. No implementation may leak a broker-native object (an MT5
struct, a Deriv contract dict) past its own boundary.

broker/base.py defines BrokerGateway: connect/disconnect/is_connected,
get_account_info, get_candles, stream_ticks, submit_order,
get_positions, get_trade_history, plus __aenter__/__aexit__ so
'async with gateway:' always disconnects, even on error.

The interface is async — tick streaming is inherently long-lived/I/O
bound, Deriv's API is a WebSocket protocol, and the target stack
already includes FastAPI (async-native). See docs/architecture.md,
'Why the interface is async', for the full rationale including the
one place this adds friction (MT5Gateway wrapping a sync SDK).

Scope is deliberately read/connect services only, per the milestone
instruction: submit_order performs no risk sizing or strategy
validation — it exists because 'order submission interface' was a
required capability, and executes exactly the request it's handed.

Adds pyproject.toml (asyncio_mode = auto) so async test functions
across the broker test suite run without per-test
@pytest.mark.asyncio.
